language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Place m oranges in n bowls on a line (one per bowl) so that no three oranges are equally spaced. Print the bowls used in ascending order.
given n : int(1..)
given m : int(1..)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..m)] of int(1..n)

branching on [x]

such that
$ the bowls are listed in ascending order, with no bowl holding two oranges
forAll i : int(1..m-1) . x[i] < x[i+1],
$ no three oranges A, B, C (in bowl order) have the distance A to B equal to the distance B to C, i.e. x[i] + x[k] is not twice x[j]
forAll i, j, k : int(1..m) . ((i < j /\ j < k) -> x[i] + x[k] != 2 * x[j])
